- button[label="{= workspace.name =}" avatar="{= workspace.initial =}" style=primary action=openHub]
- spacer
- button[label="Search" icon=search action=openSearch]
- separator
- button[label="Surfy" icon=surfy-fin action=toggleSurfy]
:::

:::tab-content[tab=docs width=880 align=center]

::::toolbar
- button[icon=chevron-left style=circled action=backToDoc tooltip="Back to the doc"]
- text[value="Editing — tidepool — Spec"]
- spacer
- button[label="Cancel" action=cancelEdit]
- button[label="Save" style=primary action=saveEditor]
::::

::::toolbar
- button[label="B" action=formatBold]
- button[label="I" action=formatItalic]
- button[label="H2" action=formatHeading]
- button[label="• List" action=formatList]
- button[label="</>" action=formatCode]
- button[label="+ Block" action=insertBlock]
::::

```markdown
## Overview

Tidepool photo gallery — static site (index.html + app.js + zip.js), Android TWA dogfood app for the builds and deployments product plan.

## Goals

- Serve the gallery as a fast static site with client-side zip download.
- Ship the same experience as an Android TWA through the Play internal-testing lane.
- Dogfood the Surfspace builds and deployments pipeline end to end.
```

+ Block inserts typed SurfDoc blocks (callout, table, model, action-items). SurfDoc source — blocks render live on save. Cancel discards; Save commits (every save is a version); autosave every 30s.

:::

::

Title-row treatment (G3 pass, WP-N3 08-11): Cancel and Save KEEP their labels — Save is the meaning-carrying primary and an icon-only ✕ beside it would read as a pane dismiss, so the pair stays textual by the G3 judgment rule (destructive-or-primary text actions keep labels). The formatting bar is a formatting bar, not a title row — its textual B / I / H2 / • List / </> / + Block buttons are unchanged by design.

::callout[type=note title="Renderer note — deferred"]
The live editing surface is `::code-editor` (planned-20), not in this train — the fenced code block stands in for the source area until it lands.
::
